    "id": "acted-fraction-instrumentation",
    "parent": "stale-accept-window-bias",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Emit acted_fraction per injected hazard so scheduler biases are measured, not guessed",
    "description": "Add a per-message 'was it acted on' counter in spur-core/src/simulator/core/exec.rs: when a delivery is dequeued, record whether the receive handler took a state-mutating branch vs. was dropped by a guard comparison, keyed by whether the message was flagged stale/orphaned by core/stale_accept.rs. Aggregate into util_stats.rs as acted_fraction (overall and restricted to biased messages) and surface it in the sequential eval metrics block alongside h1Rate/h2Rate. Gated by config field emit_acted_fraction (default true; near-zero cost, pure counter). No behavior change, no new scheduling.",
    "category": "feedback",
    "buildsOn": [
      "crash_node",
      "purgatory",
      "stale_accept"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 6,
    "rationale": "Two hypotheses in this family have been rejected without ever confirming the injected hazard was observed by the protocol. Without acted_fraction every future scheduler bias is an uncontrolled experiment; with it, a bias that fails can be attributed to either non-delivery or delivery-without-effect, which is the difference between retry and abandon.",
    "generalityArgument": "Instruments the generic dispatch path - did the handler mutate state or fall through a comparison guard - with no reference to view/term/epoch by name, so it reports for any protocol spec.",
